{
	title: 'SYSTEM.md deferred blocks, session variables and blank lines',
	spec: 'SYSTEM.md expansion leaves exactly one blank line between paragraphs: removed if blocks, comments and deferred blocks leave no gaps. Variables subagent (true/false), parent_session, fork (true/false) and fork_of describe the session; a fork records the session it was forked from. Text in <deferred>…</deferred> is left out of the system prompt so its changes never invalidate the prompt cache; the host renders it before each request and, when it differs from what the model last saw (or on the first request), appends it to the session history as a note the model reads in front of its next prompt and the transcript shows.',
	status: 'planned',
	notes: [
		'Build <updatable> inside systemPrompt.assemble(input, sources, problems), the single hookable function that builds the prompt (09-mob, task ar): prompt-trail.ts diffs the unhooked original (plugins.state.patches) against systemPrompt.inspect().text, and prompt-files.ts watches the assemble hooks. If assemble is renamed or split, keep a hookable equivalent and update both files.'
	],
	needs: ['q5', 'ar'],
